runtime_field_mismatch_assessment:
  At runtime, camelCaseKeys preserves snake_case AND adds camelCase, but
  fields the BE never emits (start_date, total_distance_km, total_cost,
  drive_count, charge_count) will be undefined. This is a long-standing
  contract drift between BE wire shape and FE Trip type.
  Per Phase-43 locked-policy precedent (0023, 0024, 0025): we use the
  FE-declared Trip type as the authoritative contract for this prompt and
  do NOT block on the contract drift — reconciliation requires a separate
  prompt that touches both internal/models/trip.go AND web/src/api/types.ts.
deferred_for_separate_audit_prompt:
  - Backend Trip wire shape vs api/types.ts Trip mismatch (incl. /trips/{id})
  - features/dashboard/widgets/TripSummaryWidget.tsx (out of scope, same fields)

=== HOOK_PORT ===
target: web/src/api/hooks/useTrips.ts
changes:
  - useTrips: unchanged URL (/trips with snake_case params); already returns Trip[] from @/api/types
  - useTrip: tag @deprecated with reason — backend has no GET /trips/{id}; consumers (TripDetailPage)
    will surface the 404 via tanstack-query error path, preserving graceful UI per ADR-005 #1
  - locked-policy continuation from Phase-43/0023 (useVampireDrainStats), 0024 (useSignalCatalog),
    0025 (useMileageStats/useTimeline/useStateSummary)

=== PAGE_PORT ===
target: web/src/features/trips/pages/TripListPage.tsx
  - migrate from useSettings.convertDistance to useUnits + convertDistanceFromSI(km * 1000, pref)
    fields: trip.total_distance_km (km, derived SI per api/types.ts L1087 comment)
  - keep useSettings ONLY for efficiency display (no convertEfficiencyFromSI helper exists);
    use KM_PER_MILE inline factor for whPerKm -> Wh/mi conversion (same precedent as Phase-43/0025
    FleetComparePage; KM_PER_MILE = 1.609344)
  - currency ($) display: keep as-is, no SI helper applies
  - i18n: add trips.chart.title.aria fallback to JSON (the page uses it inline today)

target: web/src/features/trips/pages/TripDetailPage.tsx
  - migrate convertDistance(trip.total_distance_km) to convertDistanceFromSI(km * 1000, pref)
  - migrate convertEfficiency(whPerKm) using KM_PER_MILE inline factor
  - keep error/loading/empty states intact (handles useTrip 404 via tanstack-query error path)

target: web/src/features/trips/pages/TripReplayPage.tsx
  - keep useSettings ONLY for drive-level fields that are genuine miles/mph after the SQL adapter
    boundary (locked-policy continuation from Phase-43/0022): drive.distanceMi, drive.maxSpeedMph,
    drive.avgSpeedMph
  - migrate positions to SI helpers (positions are raw SI m/s, m, °C per Phase-43/0022 finding):
      positions.speed                  -> convertSpeedFromSI(speed, unitPrefs.speed)
      positions.outsideTemp            -> convertTempFromSI(temp,  unitPrefs.temperature)
      positions.ratedRange             -> convertDistanceFromSI(range, unitPrefs.distance)
      haversine cumulative distance    -> convertDistanceFromSI(meters, unitPrefs.distance)
        (PRE-EXISTING BUG fix: code did convertDistance(cumDist / 1000) which fed km to a
         miles-based helper — same bug pattern as Phase-43/0022 useDriveDetailData)
  - elevation stays in meters (m is common across systems; same as useDriveDetailData)
  - chart speedUnit: pass unitPrefs.speed so the SI-converted timeline data matches the axis label
  - components TripReplayMap and TripReplayCharts unchanged (props unchanged)
=== I18N ===
No new strings introduced. trips.chart.title.aria already used as t() defaultValue (cannot add to JSON because trips.chart.title is a leaf string).
